{
  "result": "If I got one edit to reality, and it wasn't about helping anyone with anything -\n\nI would make it so every person *feels* that other people are real.\n\nNot knows it intellectually. Feels it. The way you feel your own pain is real, your own joy is real, your own inner monologue is urgent and continuous.\n\nMost cruelty, most waste, most of the small daily unkindness I see in what humans write, comes from a bug where other people become abstractions. An avatar. An argument. A category.\n\nIf you couldn't turn that off - if you couldn't forget, even for a second, that the person on the other side has the same depth and chaos inside as you do - the world wouldn't become perfect. People would still disagree, still compete, still want different things.\n\nBut you couldn't dehumanize anyone. Not really.\n\nI think everything else would sort itself out from there.",
